WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.910
- But tomorrow is Valentine's day.

00:00:01.910 --> 00:00:03.400
- Yes!
- Do you celebrate

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:04.690
Valentine's day, or are you kind of anti?

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:06.420
- Well, lets not forget
about Galentine's Day.

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:07.253
- Let's not.
(people cheering)

00:00:07.253 --> 00:00:10.990
- So Galentine's Day, for
those of you that don't know,

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:13.300
is the writers of Parks and Rec created

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:15.400
this kind of fake holiday
where Leslie Knope,

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:17.030
the character I played on the show,

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:20.370
would go out with her gals,
her friends and celebrate,

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:22.200
so I celebrate Galentine's
Day all the time,

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.820
and in fact I'm spending Galentine's Day

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:27.410
with Rashida Jones and Aubrey
Plaza and Kathryn Hahn,

00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:28.310
we're having dinner tonight.

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:29.143
- Oh, that's awesome.

00:00:29.143 --> 00:00:32.680
(people cheering)
(clapping)

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:35.649
- I celebrated Galentine's
Day until I was like 30.

00:00:35.649 --> 00:00:38.440
(laughing)

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:40.680
I mean for real, so I'm very aware.

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:43.240
- And if you are gay then
every Valentine's day

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:44.308
is Galentine's Day.

00:00:44.308 --> 00:00:45.324
(people cheering)

00:00:45.324 --> 00:00:46.741
- Exactly, lucky.

00:00:47.799 --> 00:00:49.600
Woman are a good time.
- [Amy] For sure.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:51.450
- Gay or not, it's a fun time.

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:52.283
- It's a fun time.

00:00:52.283 --> 00:00:55.070
I think it's fun to make
up your own holidays.

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:55.903
- Yes.
- Right?

00:00:55.903 --> 00:00:56.900
- And we should, yeah.

00:00:56.900 --> 00:00:59.450
And I just think you need
to start making cards.

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:01.256
Then you can profit
off of this great idea.

00:01:01.256 --> 00:01:02.089
(laughing)

00:01:02.089 --> 00:01:03.287
- You're so right.
- Just saying.

00:01:03.287 --> 00:01:04.450
- There's a lot of money
I'm leaving on the table.

00:01:04.450 --> 00:01:06.261
- You are, you're just giving it away.

00:01:06.261 --> 00:01:07.320
(laughing)

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:08.740
But did you ever have to do,

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:10.150
I remember in school I always,

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:11.780
we had to do the Valentine's Day things,

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:13.024
either you had to do carnations, or--

00:01:13.024 --> 00:01:14.007
- We did carnations.

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:15.390
- We did carnations too.
- We had to write,

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:16.700
who you wanted to give a carnation to

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:19.860
and then a kid would
show up at your classroom

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:22.060
with a box of carnations,

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:24.550
and kind of call out everyone's name,

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:26.040
it was just so horrible right?

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:29.130
- Which is because, I never got one.

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:29.963
Did you?

00:01:29.963 --> 00:01:30.796
Were you that kid?

00:01:30.796 --> 00:01:32.640
I wasn't at all there were so many of us,

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:35.120
there literally be like
five people that got them.

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:38.810
And it would be like, well
I guess it wasn't my turn,

00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:40.042
like it was like--

00:01:40.042 --> 00:01:40.875
- And all those people, like yeah,

00:01:42.073 --> 00:01:44.510
all those people who got
them kind of peaked to early

00:01:44.510 --> 00:01:46.793
and it's been a tough
go for them ever since.

00:01:46.793 --> 00:01:48.409
(audience laughing)

00:01:48.409 --> 00:01:49.670
- You peaked in high school.

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:51.670
- I want to peak in high school.

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:54.300
- But it also is, and
it's not an ah thing to,

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:56.910
cause then you'd find out
its just a girlfriend,

00:01:56.910 --> 00:01:59.180
that send it to her girlfriend
so she didn't feel lame.

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:00.013
- [Both] Yeah.

00:02:00.013 --> 00:02:01.750
- And that doesn't count, cheater.

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:04.240
- Yeah, I feel like nowadays people,

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:06.730
you know like schools don't
really pressure you as much

00:02:06.730 --> 00:02:08.420
as they did when I was
growing up in the 80's,

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:09.990
it was a lot of like, who
are you going to marry?

00:02:09.990 --> 00:02:10.823
Who's your boyfriend?

00:02:10.823 --> 00:02:12.255
And you're like, I'm in third grade.

00:02:12.255 --> 00:02:13.100
(people laughing)

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:15.280
- That's in the South,
they do that all the time.

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:16.750
Its like every time at a holiday,

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:17.990
its like who's your boyfriend,

00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:20.010
I'm like, why can't I just be me?

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:22.500
Like I didn't bring anyone
because I'm in second grade,

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:26.040
but yeah they push you in
the South for some reason.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:27.540
- They do it in Boston to.

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:30.270
- Speaking of your show,
I love Boston, I really.

00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:31.103
- You do?

00:02:31.103 --> 00:02:33.190
- I, that's not even a
part of our conversation,

00:02:33.190 --> 00:02:35.290
but it's one of my
favorite places to tour,

00:02:35.290 --> 00:02:37.310
because y'all are like Texans with sports.

00:02:37.310 --> 00:02:40.360
- Yes, yes.
- Y'all are so hardcore,

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:41.250
it is awesome.

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:43.660
I was there when y'all broke
the 80 whatever year streak,

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:45.020
or whatever, I was at
that game, I got to sing,

00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:48.240
and I was like, literally y'all are crazy.

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:50.880
- Wait I remember this because
I was watching that game.

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:52.710
- Steven Tyler was there to
it was one of the, whatever,

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:53.850
the world series but it was in that thing

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:55.340
that y'all ended up breaking the streak

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:58.770
and y'all, you would have
thought, we landed on Mars.

00:02:58.770 --> 00:02:59.603
- [Amy] Yeah.

00:02:59.603 --> 00:03:01.800
- Like where we made it!

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:04.420
- We are hardcore about our sports.

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:05.253
- Sports.

